{"module":"environment","voice":"male","duration":184.7,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Environmental racism: who breathes the dirty air","start":0.0,"end":3.36,"words":[[0.04,1.1],[1.1,1.79],[2.05,2.21],[2.21,2.58],[2.58,2.74],[2.74,3.04],[3.04,3.19]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The same maps that show redlining and urban renewal often show where the landfills, refineries and highways went.","start":4.16,"end":11.63,"words":[[4.21,4.36],[4.36,4.68],[4.68,4.99],[4.99,5.23],[5.23,5.47],[5.47,6.17],[6.17,6.41],[6.41,6.73],[6.73,7.28],[7.28,7.59],[7.59,7.83],[7.83,8.06],[8.06,8.22],[8.22,8.93],[9.21,9.99],[9.99,10.23],[10.23,10.78],[10.78,11.17]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Pollution is another way place decides health and wealth.","start":11.98,"end":15.41,"words":[[12.03,12.52],[12.52,12.65],[12.65,13.0],[13.0,13.21],[13.21,13.55],[13.55,14.04],[14.04,14.32],[14.32,14.52],[14.52,14.87]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Where the movement started","start":15.76,"end":17.39,"words":[[15.8,16.04],[16.04,16.21],[16.21,16.78],[16.78,17.27]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 1982, residents of mostly Black Warren County, North Carolina, lay down in the road to stop trucks carrying soil contaminated with PCBs to a new landfill; more than 500 people were arrested.","start":18.09,"end":32.26,"words":[[18.14,18.29],[18.29,19.33],[19.59,20.26],[20.26,20.41],[20.41,20.93],[20.93,21.23],[21.23,21.6],[21.6,22.12],[22.38,22.6],[22.6,23.35],[23.61,23.83],[23.83,24.13],[24.13,24.28],[24.28,24.42],[24.42,24.72],[24.72,24.87],[24.87,25.17],[25.17,25.54],[25.54,26.06],[26.06,26.36],[26.36,27.32],[27.32,27.55],[27.55,27.99],[27.99,28.14],[28.14,28.29],[28.29,28.51],[28.51,29.11],[29.37,29.52],[29.52,29.74],[29.74,30.56],[30.56,30.93],[30.93,31.08],[31.08,31.67]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In 1987 the United Church of Christ's report Toxic Wastes and Race found that race was the strongest predictor of where hazardous waste facilities were located in the U.S.","start":32.61,"end":43.68,"words":[[32.67,32.81],[32.81,33.96],[33.96,34.1],[34.1,34.67],[34.67,35.03],[35.03,35.17],[35.17,35.68],[35.68,36.03],[36.03,36.46],[36.46,36.89],[36.89,37.11],[37.11,37.4],[37.4,37.75],[37.75,37.97],[37.97,38.25],[38.25,38.47],[38.47,38.61],[38.61,39.26],[39.26,39.83],[39.83,39.97],[39.97,40.19],[40.19,40.69],[40.69,41.05],[41.05,41.69],[41.69,41.84],[41.84,42.48],[42.48,42.62],[42.62,42.77],[42.77,43.13]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Cancer Alley","start":44.58,"end":45.62,"words":[[44.6,45.13],[45.13,45.44]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Along about 85 miles of the Mississippi River between Baton Rouge and New Orleans sit well over a hundred petrochemical plants and refineries, many next to Black communities founded by freed people.","start":46.32,"end":60.28,"words":[[46.36,46.68],[46.68,47.09],[47.09,47.75],[47.75,48.16],[48.16,48.32],[48.32,48.48],[48.48,49.14],[49.14,49.46],[49.46,49.95],[49.95,50.36],[50.36,50.61],[50.61,50.85],[50.85,51.1],[51.1,51.59],[51.59,51.84],[51.84,52.08],[52.08,52.41],[52.41,52.57],[52.57,53.14],[53.14,54.21],[54.21,54.7],[54.7,54.94],[54.94,55.84],[56.13,56.45],[56.45,56.86],[56.86,57.03],[57.03,57.35],[57.35,58.17],[58.17,58.74],[58.74,58.99],[58.99,59.32],[59.32,59.81]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In 2014 the EPA estimated that census tracts near the Denka chloroprene plant in LaPlace had among the highest cancer risks from air toxics in the country.","start":60.63,"end":71.11,"words":[[60.68,60.84],[60.84,61.7],[61.7,61.86],[61.86,62.09],[62.09,62.87],[62.87,63.11],[63.11,63.58],[63.58,64.04],[64.04,64.28],[64.28,64.43],[64.43,64.83],[64.83,65.61],[65.61,66.0],[66.0,66.15],[66.15,66.7],[66.7,66.94],[66.94,67.25],[67.25,67.4],[67.4,67.87],[67.87,68.26],[68.26,68.65],[68.65,68.97],[68.97,69.12],[69.12,69.67],[69.67,69.83],[69.83,69.98],[69.98,70.53]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Flint","start":72.01,"end":72.74,"words":[[72.05,72.57]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In April 2014, state-appointed managers switched majority-Black Flint, Michigan, to river water without proper corrosion control, and lead leached into homes for more than a year while officials dismissed residents' complaints.","start":73.44,"end":89.05,"words":[[73.48,73.63],[73.63,74.09],[74.09,75.01],[75.27,76.27],[76.27,76.88],[76.88,77.34],[77.34,78.33],[78.33,78.79],[79.05,79.67],[79.93,80.09],[80.09,80.39],[80.39,80.7],[80.7,81.16],[81.16,81.54],[81.54,82.15],[82.15,82.84],[83.1,83.33],[83.33,83.56],[83.56,83.94],[83.94,84.25],[84.25,84.63],[84.63,84.78],[84.78,84.94],[84.94,85.17],[85.17,85.32],[85.32,85.55],[85.55,85.85],[85.85,86.39],[86.39,86.92],[86.92,87.61],[87.61,88.45]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The Michigan Civil Rights Commission concluded in 2017 that systemic racism played a role.","start":89.4,"end":95.92,"words":[[89.45,89.6],[89.6,90.1],[90.1,90.47],[90.47,90.83],[90.83,91.33],[91.33,91.99],[91.99,92.13],[92.13,93.14],[93.14,93.36],[93.36,93.94],[93.94,94.52],[94.52,94.88],[94.88,95.03],[95.03,95.39]]},{"el":"s2","text":"A settlement of about $626 million was approved in 2021.","start":96.27,"end":102.4,"words":[[96.32,96.46],[96.46,97.1],[97.1,97.24],[97.24,97.6],[97.6,99.51],[99.51,99.94],[99.94,100.15],[100.15,100.58],[100.58,100.72],[100.72,101.86]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Air and heat","start":103.3,"end":105.15,"words":[[103.34,103.76],[103.76,104.4],[104.4,105.03]]},{"el":"s3","text":"A 2019 study in PNAS found that Black and Hispanic Americans breathe more fine-particle pollution than is caused by their own consumption, while white Americans breathe less.","start":105.85,"end":118.0,"words":[[105.89,106.06],[106.06,107.13],[107.13,107.54],[107.54,107.71],[107.71,108.12],[108.12,108.53],[108.53,108.78],[108.78,109.11],[109.11,109.36],[109.36,110.02],[110.02,110.76],[110.76,111.09],[111.09,111.26],[111.26,112.16],[112.16,112.74],[112.74,112.99],[112.99,113.15],[113.15,113.48],[113.48,113.73],[113.73,113.98],[113.98,114.23],[114.23,115.13],[115.42,115.75],[115.75,116.08],[116.08,116.82],[116.82,117.15],[117.15,117.48]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Highways built through Black neighborhoods (see “Burned, flooded and taken”) brought traffic pollution, and formerly redlined areas run hotter in summer (see the module on place).","start":118.35,"end":129.32,"words":[[118.4,118.95],[118.95,119.27],[119.27,119.5],[119.5,119.82],[119.82,120.53],[120.53,120.69],[120.69,121.08],[121.36,121.84],[121.84,122.07],[122.07,122.55],[122.82,123.14],[123.14,123.61],[123.61,124.25],[124.52,124.76],[124.76,125.23],[125.23,125.86],[125.86,126.34],[126.34,126.58],[126.58,126.89],[126.89,127.05],[127.05,127.37],[127.37,127.52],[127.52,127.68],[127.68,128.16],[128.16,128.31],[128.31,128.79]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Intent or economics?","start":130.22,"end":132.31,"words":[[130.27,130.8],[130.8,130.89],[130.89,131.78]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Researchers debate why facilities end up near communities of color.","start":133.01,"end":137.72,"words":[[133.1,133.73],[133.73,134.21],[134.21,134.45],[134.45,135.16],[135.16,135.4],[135.4,135.56],[135.56,135.79],[135.79,136.59],[136.59,136.75],[136.75,137.14]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Some evidence shows they were deliberately placed where residents had the least political power.","start":138.07,"end":143.31,"words":[[138.12,138.32],[138.32,138.78],[138.78,139.05],[139.05,139.24],[139.24,139.38],[139.38,140.1],[140.1,140.5],[140.5,140.69],[140.69,141.29],[141.29,141.48],[141.48,141.62],[141.62,141.88],[141.88,142.47],[142.47,142.8]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Other studies find that, in some places, poorer residents moved in after facilities were built because land and housing became cheap.","start":143.66,"end":152.83,"words":[[143.71,143.95],[143.95,144.44],[144.44,144.85],[144.85,145.17],[145.46,145.62],[145.62,145.86],[145.86,146.51],[146.8,147.2],[147.2,147.93],[147.93,148.26],[148.26,148.42],[148.42,148.75],[148.75,149.48],[149.48,149.64],[149.64,149.97],[149.97,150.37],[150.37,150.7],[150.7,150.94],[150.94,151.43],[151.43,151.92],[151.92,152.32]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Both paths lead to the same unequal exposure.","start":153.18,"end":156.62,"words":[[153.23,153.55],[153.55,153.87],[153.87,154.11],[154.11,154.28],[154.28,154.44],[154.44,154.76],[154.76,155.32],[155.32,156.04]]},{"el":"h5","text":"What helps","start":157.52,"end":158.41,"words":[[157.57,157.8],[157.8,158.19]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Communities have won by organizing, testing their own air and water, and suing.","start":159.11,"end":165.1,"words":[[159.16,159.98],[159.98,160.22],[160.22,160.47],[160.47,160.71],[160.71,161.53],[161.81,162.3],[162.3,162.54],[162.54,162.79],[162.79,162.95],[162.95,163.2],[163.2,163.6],[163.89,164.13],[164.13,164.54]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Federal environmental justice programs expanded under the Justice40 initiative (2021) and were largely rolled back in 2025, so state and local action matters more.","start":165.45,"end":179.23,"words":[[165.48,166.05],[166.05,167.19],[167.19,167.76],[167.76,168.5],[168.5,169.23],[169.23,169.56],[169.56,169.72],[169.72,170.62],[170.62,171.35],[171.35,172.57],[172.86,173.1],[173.1,173.26],[173.26,173.75],[173.75,174.16],[174.16,174.41],[174.41,174.57],[174.57,175.95],[176.24,176.48],[176.48,176.89],[176.89,177.14],[177.14,177.62],[177.62,178.03],[178.03,178.44],[178.44,178.68]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Show up at permit hearings; they are often decided by who attends.","start":179.58,"end":183.75,"words":[[179.63,179.84],[179.84,179.98],[179.98,180.12],[180.12,180.47],[180.47,181.02],[181.26,181.47],[181.47,181.54],[181.54,181.82],[181.82,182.37],[182.37,182.58],[182.58,182.72],[182.72,183.21]]}]}